show that the certificate is not necessary for successful BFGS behavior. The
planar application below shows a different point: moving geometry can prove
convergence where the fixed radial field fails.


4 Global convergence: homogeneous and mixed geometry

Toward a minimizer, a homogeneous term has an exact first-order model; a
smooth convex term adds only a quadratic remainder. We turn this inward
accuracy into the secant bound needed by the comparison energy, then apply it
to centered sums and coercive homogeneous objectives in any finite dimension.


4.1 Why inward accuracy controls a nonradial algorithm

A gradient jump can make the positive correction in (6) large. We control its
pairing with the direction to a minimizer by asking that first-order prediction
remain quadratically accurate on short inward segments. This asks nothing
