4.2 A family theorem and the mixed benchmark

A finite convex positively homogeneous function is sublinear: its value on
(1 − τ )r is exactly (1 − τ ) times its value on r. Its angular nonsmoothness
consequently disappears from the inward remainder. The next theorem permits
an arbitrary locally C 1,1 convex perturbation, provided the homogeneous part
is centered at a minimizer of the sum. Centering is a geometric hypothesis on
the objective, not knowledge required by the algorithm. In particular, the two
summands need not separately be minimized at that center.

